{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Create national guidance for \u2018Slow for Cats\u2019 warning signs in rural communities",
        "additional_details": "Domestic cats are killed or injured on roads in villages and rural areas annually. There is no national system for recording cat road deaths in place.\r\n\r\nCats are not included in road traffic casualty statistics, and there is no requirement for incidents involving pets to be reported. As a result, local authorities lack consistent evidence to identify high-risk areas.\r\n\r\nRural communities have high numbers of free roaming cats, with fast-moving country roads. This can lead to preventable collisions.",
        "background": "Introduce national guidance for local authorities to install \u201cSlow for Cats\u201d warning signs and related traffic-calming measures in rural and semi-rural areas where there is evidence of frequent domestic cat road deaths.",
